"""
# Driver capsule identity, parallel codegen pool, HIR residency, determinism, and cache memory

Tests five invariants across driver and MIR lowering:
1. `compute_native_capsule_mir_identity_v1` streams SHA-256 incrementally without
   a giant `rows.join("\n")` transient buffer, matches canonical row-join SHA-256
   byte-for-byte, and `driver_aot_native_output` distinguishes empty recompute
   failure from actual MIR mutation.
2. `_driver_codegen_pool_lane_reason_v1` unlocks the parallel codegen pool for
   built-in static `llvm` even when `backend_session` is open (`plugin_path == ""`),
   while keeping custom plugins and non-LLVM backends serial; eviction preserves
   `--output-format both`.
3. `hir_function_keeps_body_in_module_v1` preserves function bodies on per-module
   `nogc_strict` modules while keeping `mir_shard_hir_residency_refusal_v1`
   spec-compatible.
4. Lambda lifting in `switch_operators_calls.spl` uses a deterministic per-module
   counter and module hash/fold tag so parallel MIR shard claim orders never alter
   lifted names or collide.
5. `hir_source_text_hash_cache` keys on content digests instead of raw source text,
   and `driver_entry_scan_cache_reset` / `driver_entry_scan_cache_release` release
   `_g_entry_scan_content_by_path` after closure sources are scanned.
"""
# @req REQ-DRIVER-CODEGEN-POOL-AND-RESIDENCY
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/native_capsule_mir_identity.spl
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_aot_native_output.spl
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_mir_shard_hir_residency_v1.spl
# @cover src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/switch_operators_calls.spl
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_hir_cache.spl
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_entry_closure_core.spl

